[38;5;231m⏺[39m I added a basic checkbox to [38;5;153mindex.html[39m. It's a standard HTML checkbox wrapped in a [38;5;153m<label>[39m, so clicking the text
  toggles it too:

  [90m<[34mmain[90m>[39m
    [90m<[34mlabel[90m>[39m
      [90m<[34minput[90m [36mtype[90m=[31m"checkbox"[90m [36mname[90m=[31m"done"[90m>[39m
      Example task
    [90m</[34mlabel[90m>[39m
  [90m</[34mmain[90m>[39m

  The browser handles the on/off state, so there's no JavaScript or CSS. I haven't opened it in a browser.

  The page had no items yet, so I used "Example task" as a placeholder; rename it or copy the [38;5;153m<label>[39m block for each
  item. The checked state resets when the page reloads. If you want it to persist, or want finished items crossed out, I
  can add that.

